From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Dalessio <mike.dalessio@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 14 Jun 2026 18:41:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix: Document#root= rejects non-element nodes

A DTD could be assigned as the document root. An unlinked DTD is freed
directly during teardown, but assigning it as root also relinks it into
the tree, so xmlFreeDoc frees it a second time -- a heap use-after-free.

Restrict root= to element nodes, raising TypeError otherwise. The
type check now happens before the current root is unlinked/pinned, so
a rejected assignment leaves the document's existing root untouched.

ref: https://github.com/sparklemotion/nokogiri/security/advisories/GHSA-wjv4-x9w8-wm3h

Fixes: CVE-2026-57436

[Shivani: backported to nokogiri-1.13.6. Same fix, adapted to this
version's plain Data_Get_Struct (no Noko_Node_Get_Struct macro exists
here). Dropped the JRuby XmlDocument.java hunk (not shipped in this
package) and test changes. Reproduced the double-free
("double free or corruption (!prev)") on the unpatched 1.13.6 C
extension by unlinking a DTD node and assigning it via
Document#root=, and confirmed this patch converts it into a clean
TypeError while leaving the original root intact.]
Signed-off-by: Shivani Agarwal <shivani.agarwal@broadcom.com>
---
 ext/nokogiri/xml_document.c | 30 +++++++++++++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ext/nokogiri/xml_document.c b/ext/nokogiri/xml_document.c
index 20a9e40..39c87c5 100644
--- a/ext/nokogiri/xml_document.c
+++ b/ext/nokogiri/xml_document.c
@@ -148,12 +148,6 @@ rb_xml_document_root_set(VALUE self, VALUE rb_new_root)
 
   Data_Get_Struct(self, xmlDoc, c_document);
 
-  c_current_root = xmlDocGetRootElement(c_document);
-  if (c_current_root) {
-    xmlUnlinkNode(c_current_root);
-    noko_xml_document_pin_node(c_current_root);
-  }
-
   if (!NIL_P(rb_new_root)) {
     if (!rb_obj_is_kind_of(rb_new_root, cNokogiriXmlNode)) {
       rb_raise(rb_eArgError,
@@ -163,13 +157,23 @@ rb_xml_document_root_set(VALUE self, VALUE rb_new_root)
 
     Data_Get_Struct(rb_new_root, xmlNode, c_new_root);
 
-    /* If the new root's document is not the same as the current document,
-     * then we need to dup the node in to this document. */
-    if (c_new_root->doc != c_document) {
-      c_new_root = xmlDocCopyNode(c_new_root, c_document, 1);
-      if (!c_new_root) {
-        rb_raise(rb_eRuntimeError, "Could not reparent node (xmlDocCopyNode)");
-      }
+    if (c_new_root->type != XML_ELEMENT_NODE) {
+      rb_raise(rb_eTypeError, "root must be a Nokogiri::XML::Element");
+    }
+  }
+
+  c_current_root = xmlDocGetRootElement(c_document);
+  if (c_current_root) {
+    xmlUnlinkNode(c_current_root);
+    noko_xml_document_pin_node(c_current_root);
+  }
+
+  /* If the new root's document is not the same as the current document,
+   * then we need to dup the node in to this document. */
+  if (c_new_root && c_new_root->doc != c_document) {
+    c_new_root = xmlDocCopyNode(c_new_root, c_document, 1);
+    if (!c_new_root) {
+      rb_raise(rb_eRuntimeError, "Could not reparent node (xmlDocCopyNode)");
     }
   }
 
